From adbdee1ea7850ca9d8e92a49ade01b532ffcdc40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:40:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] drm/panfrost: Don't WARN for a heap folio a
 neighbouring chunk filled

panfrost_mmu_map_fault_addr() fills the page array of a heap BO a whole
folio at a time, aligned down to the start of the folio, and warns when
it finds a page of the folio already filled in. With 16K or 64K pages,
the THP mount panfrost uses for its BOs can return folios larger than
the 2 MB fault chunk (up to 32 MB and 128 MB). The first fault in such
a folio fills the entries of the neighbouring chunks too, so every later
fault in one of those chunks finds the folio's pages already owned and
WARNs, although all it has to do is drop the extra folio reference it
took, as it does.

Warn only for a folio that fits in the chunk: its pages can only have
been filled by an earlier fault in the same chunk, which is a bug.

Not reproduced: with 4K pages, as here, a folio is at most 2 MB and
never crosses a chunk.

Fixes: b49c35ba0ce1 ("drm/panfrost: Fix a page leak in panfrost_mmu_map_fault_addr() when THP is on")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/all/sashiko-outbox-210837@kernel.org/
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
index c9ade97..9b7591b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
@@ -715,11 +715,13 @@ static int panfrost_mmu_map_fault_addr(struct panfrost_device *pfdev, int as,
 			pages[pg++] = folio_page(folio, i);
 		}
 
-		/* We always fill the page array at a folio granularity so
-		 * there's no valid reason for a folio range to be partially
-		 * populated.
+		/* We always fill the page array at a folio granularity, so a
+		 * folio is already owned only if it is larger than the chunk
+		 * and the fault of a neighbouring chunk filled it.
 		 */
-		if (drm_WARN_ON(&pfdev->base, already_owned)) {
+		if (already_owned) {
+			drm_WARN_ON(&pfdev->base,
+				    folio_nr_pages(folio) <= NUM_FAULT_PAGES);
 			folio_put(folio);
 		} else {
 			got_start = min(got_start, first);
-- 
